# English app text

- Every piece of text the app itself shows is English: labels, buttons, titles, headings, tabs, menus, toasts,
  popups and dialogs (their titles, messages and buttons), tooltips, empty-state texts, error messages and the
  screen-reader labels. Do not add Persian to any of these.
- Use plain, easy English. Short sentences, common words. Say what the learner must do and what happens next.
  Avoid fancy or formal words (for example write "Finish" not "Complete the prerequisite", "Close" not "Dismiss").
  A learner should understand every line without a dictionary.
- Buttons and dialogs: use short English labels such as `OK`, `Close`, `Cancel`, `Start`, `Back`.
- Learner content stays as it is: the Persian sentence to translate, Persian meanings, Persian hints and Persian
  grammar explanations come from the lesson files and are not app text. Do not translate them into English.
- When you add a new message or label to the app, write it in English first. Do not leave a Persian placeholder.
